WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.520
When living conditions worsen and the economy&nbsp;
fails, people try to find reasons for their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:11.200
troubles. This is when political extremists&nbsp;
can become popular as they blame certain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:18.720
groups of people and promise that by getting&nbsp;
rid of them societies’ problems will go away.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:23.440
This can lead to the deliberate elimination of&nbsp;
those who are different because of their race,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:29.960
religion, sexuality, or disability&nbsp;
- a phenomenon known as genocide.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:40.400
The 10 stages of genocide are a framework for&nbsp;
understanding how crimes against humanity happen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:46.480
so we can spot early warning signs&nbsp;
and potentially prevent them.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:51.000
Stage one is classification:&nbsp;
Extremists divide people into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:55.600
separate groups based on their different&nbsp;
characteristics. This often happens to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:03.120
create an us-vs-them mentality or find&nbsp;
someone to blame for social problems.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:09.240
The second stage is symbolization: This involves&nbsp;
assigning symbols or names to members of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:17.560
other group. The goal here is to split the&nbsp;
society and make it clear who belongs to who.

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:22.760
3rd is discrimination: The dominant&nbsp;
group uses its power to deny others&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:27.920
certain rights or privileges. Particular&nbsp;
new laws may limit the freedom of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:36.160
marginalized ones. Instances of bullying&nbsp;
increase and the societal divide widens.

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:41.960
4th is dehumanization: the targeted&nbsp;
group is portrayed as less than human,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:46.760
often compared to animals or diseases.&nbsp;
Stripping away the human qualities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:52.920
of a person makes it easier to&nbsp;
justify violence against them.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:58.200
5th is organization: This stage can&nbsp;
involve violent mobs that are tolerated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:04.640
by the ruling class or even the creation of&nbsp;
state-sponsored militias. In some instances,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:11.560
perpetrators now carefully start to&nbsp;
plan the next steps of the genocide.

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:17.160
6th is polarization: Extremists now&nbsp;
demonize the targeted group and try&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:23.360
to fully divide society by demanding that&nbsp;
everyone must take a side. Moderators who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:29.760
want to reduce the tensions are often&nbsp;
identified as enemies and silenced.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:37.800
7th is preparation. The criminals now plan&nbsp;
for mass murder. They may identify victims by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:46.400
name or number, find where they live and acquire&nbsp;
weapons or build facilities to aid their efforts.

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:51.200
8th is persecution: Violence&nbsp;
escalates. The targeted group&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:54.880
is systematically subjected&nbsp;
to harassment, displacement,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.880 --> 00:03:03.160
or other forms of abuse. Often all of that&nbsp;
happens under the disguise of security measures.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:10.560
9th is extermination. The mass killing begins. The&nbsp;
culprits view their victims as less than human,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:14.240
believing they are "cleansing" the&nbsp;
world of an undesirable element,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:20.640
and in doing so justify the use&nbsp;
of disproportionate violence.

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:28.080
10th is denial. Those responsible for the cruelty&nbsp;
deny their crimes, destroy evidence, blame the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:36.800
victims, and attempt to rewrite history justifying&nbsp;
their actions as necessary for the greater good.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:42.000
This is why in the aftermath of genocide, the&nbsp;
criminals must be made accountable and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:50.760
trauma must be addressed. Then the survivors&nbsp;
may heal and society can attempt to reunite.

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:58.560
Note that the 10 stages may not occur&nbsp;
linearly. They can happen simultaneously.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:01.800
Dr. Gregory Stanton, who observed the phenomenon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:06.520
suggested preventative measures to battle&nbsp;
each stage, even though he believed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:13.520
that ultimately only an international&nbsp;
intervention can stop such a disaster.

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:19.400
In Germany, Cambodia, Rwanda, and other&nbsp;
places, help from outside often arrived&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:24.760
too late for too many, which is why&nbsp;
Stanton also founded Genocide Watch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:29.600
a nonprofit to help prevent the&nbsp;
next tragedy from unfolding.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:37.600
What do you think? Is knowledge enough to prevent&nbsp;
genocidal events? And if not, what other measures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:59.840
can we take to avoid the next human catastrophe?&nbsp;
